I tried it in explore mode: unencumbered, with only a cavewoman's
starting inventory, I didn't lose HP when I went down a level by wand
of digging. Trying other possibilities in explore mode just now, I
found that xanthian was wrong: you don't lose HP if you fall down a
self-dug hole when you're burdened either. Or when you fall down an
already existing hole burdened or unburdened, for that matter. Perhaps
he's confused about falling down the stairs when you're burdened or
fumbling; that may indeed kill you when you're low on HP.

The only difference between a hole you make and a hole that's already
there is that if you dig down, you go down immediately at the spot
you're standing instead of having to step into (or stumble on) the
hole. 

